# Incident debugging with a trace

Invoke with `@incident-debug` when given an error code + `trace_id` (or a user report that
implies one).

1. Open the trace in Langfuse; identify the failing span (node) and generation (LLM call),
   if any.
2. Check which terminal state was reached (`03-harness-loop-and-termination.mdc`) and which
   rung of the failure ladder fired (`14-provider-abstraction-mcp.mdc`).
3. Check whether a checkpoint exists for the job — can it resume, or does it need a manual
   re-run?
4. Check budget state (iterations/time/tokens/USD) and circuit-breaker state for the
   dependency involved — was this a genuine failure or a budget/circuit-break trip?
5. Write up findings using `docs/playbooks/incident-response-playbook.md`, referencing the
   `trace_id` directly rather than re-describing what the trace shows.
